{
 "_what": "Fingerprints are keyed by stable release source path, independent of deployed destination. Read only to migrate a harness that has no installed-file receipt: a destination whose fingerprint is not listed under its source key is not recognised as Orion's and is preserved. Contract: update/manifest.json deployment and agent/updating.md.",
 "_fingerprint": "SHA-256, as lowercase hex, of the file read as UTF-8 text with every CRLF turned into LF.",
 "_frozen": "Frozen compatibility data for 2.0.0 harnesses installed before installed-file receipts: one fingerprint per file, its last 2.0.0 version before receipts (commit 55d0e65). 1.x harnesses are reinstalled, never updated (agent/reinstall-from-1.x.md), so no older version is listed. Never regenerated from git history and never extended with the bytes of a release edit. update/release-contract.mjs validates its structure and that every retirement identity in update/manifest.json is listed. It lists no versions of itself: updates read only the incoming release's copy, so a harness's copy is bookkeeping, replaced whatever its bytes.",
